<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Qaboos bin Said</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1940">1940</a>–<a href="/years/2020">2020</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Qaboos bin Said was sultan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oman">Oman</a> from 1970 to 2020, the longest-serving ruler in the Arab world at his death. He deposed his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/said-bin-taimur">Said bin Taimur</a>, renamed the country the Sultanate of Oman, defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dhofar">Dhofar</a> rebellion and used oil revenue to build roads, schools and hospitals. Abroad he followed a neutral policy and often acted as a mediator.</p></div>
